# J1 — Keyless first launch (⭐ highest priority)
# Persona: brand-new user, no credentials. Confirm a target, inspect aggregate
# Setup's plan-dependent readiness, then take the `demo` offline escape hatch.
name: Keyless first launch
note: HOME is redirected to a temp dir. Keychain/OAuth-cached credentials cannot be masked from here — if the auth gate never appears, check for cached credentials before judging.
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY OPENROUTER_API_KEY GEMINI_API_KEY
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch:
wait-for: 25 CHOOSE A TARGET
snap: target-gate
expect: Nothing defaults to cwd silently
expect: :demo
ask: Target gate — is the operator told WHY they are stopped here, and is the next action obvious without docs?
keys: Enter
wait-for: 5 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN
snap: aggregate-setup
expect: Model          NOT NEEDED
expect: Credentials    NOT NEEDED
expect: Start Map      READY
ask: Aggregate Setup — can a keyless user tell why this deterministic plan needs neither a model nor credentials, and is the single Start Map commit obvious?
submit: demo
wait-for: 120 run completed
# The completed run parks a RESULT READY card whose advertised keys are
# Navigate-mode only (app/phase_results.rs: `n` Use & Review, `u` Use scan,
# `o` Open, `r` Run again). Converge on Navigate first — sent from Prompt the
# key is just typed into the composer. Accepting routes to the derived next
# phase, so the top bar leaves "Viewing Scan".
nav-mode
keys: n
wait-for: 20 Viewing Map
submit: findings
wait-for: 20 REVIEW VIEW
snap: offline-demo-result
expect: findings
expect: signal
# Location facets carry a per-fixture tally, so assert the redacted file, not
# its count.
expect: config.env
ask: Offline escape hatch — did `demo` make a real scanner signal, redacted location, and signal_only proof state legible, not just dump logs?
